notes="This landscape music-paper leaf is headed Th Eilenberg-Zilber-Cartier, with EZ1 and a cancelled EZ2. It states natural comparison morphisms for a bisimplicial abelian object, homotopies, higher choices, then gives shuffle and Alexander-Whitney trials and a cup-product consequence. The spelling bisimplical and masculine evidents after fleches are retained. The first pair visibly has phi going from integral N to NDelta and psi returning. With ordinary right-to-left composition, the immediately following phi psi~1_integral N and psi phi~1_NDelta have reversed domains; the later psi phi and phi psi displays, and the dk/dh equations, have the usual domains. No labels are exchanged in the transcription. A second issue is the written plus in k'-k=d ell+ell d and h'-h=dm+md: for a degree2 ell and differential d of degree-1, the usual Hom differential gives d ell-ell d. Direct expansion gives d(d ell+ell d)+(d ell+ell d)d=2d ell d, so the displayed plus is not automatically a degree1 cycle. The page does not specify a convention resolving this; the plus remains. The low alpha beside the short-shuffle coefficient is marked doubtful rather than silently raised. The hatted d acquires a visible prime in its iterated definition, though the preceding AW trial lacks it. The signed AW expression and cup-product trial have not been independently proved here. The cup trial writes n+1 on the first line and ends at xn on the second, and leaves the exponent of (-1) unwritten. The large point picture includes two very faint middle connectors; these are retained with medium confidence. Foot358, no date. MacLane is a manuscript citation only; no cited work was consulted."
commit(n,t,ds,cc,items,notes,hand=['Tall looped b can resemble l: the title favors Zilber. The spelling bisimplical lacks the expected extra i after c and is not normalized.','A final t can flow directly into s: evidents is written despite the feminine noun fleches.','Printed music staff lines are gray and continue across the sheet; cf MacLane has three separate blue underline strokes, while Homology has none.','Some arrow shafts are doubled or repeated without an added label; the degree-one k map has two right heads.','The isolated and terminal xi1 use a serifed upright1, contrasting with the dotted i.'],notation=[('phi/psi','First pair: phi right, psi left; subsequent domain mismatch in homotopy line retained.'),('hat d prime','Prime appears in the iterated last-face definition, not silently inserted in the earlier AW trial.'),('vertical equality ticks','Two strokes between raised n and i+j.'),('Z X','Plain Z in the chain-object display.'),('x_i1','Both short-shuffle trial occurrences have second index1.')],abbr=[('Th','Théorème'),('eq de cat','équivalence de catégories'),('q ism','quasi-isomorphisme'),('degen homot triv','dégénérés homotopiquement triviaux'),('fonct','fonctoriels'),('t.q.','tel que'),('op face','opérateur face'),('op simpl.','opérateur simplicial'),('comm.','commutatif'),('anticom.','anticommutatif')],checks=[check('357.composition-domains','From the drawn first pair, phi:integral N to NDelta and psi:NDelta to integral N. Thus psi phi acts on integral N, phi psi on NDelta. The first written homotopy line has these domains reversed; later formulas match.','targeted proof check'),check('357.higher-homotopy-sign','Expanded d(d ell+ell d)+(d ell+ell d)d with d squared zero: result2d ell d. The usual degree2 boundary d ell-ell d instead gives zero. This diagnoses a convention/sign issue, not a correction of the ink.','targeted proof check')],unresolved=[additional_doubt('cancelled N trial',r'N:\mathrm{Ab}(\text{bisimpl.})\to A(',confidence='low',evidence='The middle letters lie under dense crossing; cancel_N crop.'),additional_doubt('cancelled composition trial',r'\varphi\psi(X_{**})',confidence='low',evidence='Crowded crossed loops in the native left half.'),additional_doubt('cancelled shuffle coefficient',r'\sum(-1)s_\alpha s\prime_\beta(',confidence='low',evidence='Two diagonal crossings obscure the parenthesized sign; cancel_shuffle crop.'),additional_doubt('short-shuffle alpha placement',r'(-1)_\alpha',alternatives=r'(-1)^\alpha',confidence='low',evidence='The small alpha is low beside the coefficient; xi_sum crop.'),additional_doubt('point-label deleted marks','0 in each label',confidence='low',evidence='Hatch obscures the original closed traces in both labels; graph crop.')])
